0	section	Talking to Cassius again before talking to both Gillie and Seth
1	line	Player	What was it you needed me to do again?
1	line	Cassius	I need you to speak to Gillie and Seth Groats. We need to learn everything we can.
1	line	Cassius	They live just across the River Lum. Head east from here and you should be able to find them.
0	section	Talking to Gillie
1	line	Gillie Groats	Hello, I'm Gillie the Milkmaid. What can I do for you?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Who are you?
1	option	Can you tell me how to milk a cow?
1	option	Can you share what makes your cows so productive?
2	line	Player	Can you share what makes your cows so productive?
2	line	Gillie Groats	Absolutely! The secret is happiness.
2	line	Player	Happiness?
2	line	Gillie Groats	The cows make the best milk when they're happy, and to be honest, they make too much!
2	line	Gillie Groats	I'm always glad that adventurers come by and help with milking them. I wouldn't be able to keep up otherwise.
2	line	Player	That can't be everything though, can it?
2	line	Gillie Groats	Come to think of it, I'm sure my father keeps a few tricks up his sleeve. Why don't you go and ask him?
2	cond	If the player has not yet talked to Seth Groats:
3	line	Player	That would be Seth, wouldn't it?
3	line	Gillie Groats	It would be! I'm sure he'll he happy to share some information with you.
3	line	Player	I'll go and speak to him now, thank you!
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has already talked to Seth Groats:
3	line	Player	I've already had a chance to talk to him. He did indeed have some tricks to share!
3	line	Gillie Groats	That's good. You must be ready to care for your own cows at this point!
3	line	Player	If you think so, then I must be. Thank you for your help, I'll make sure that knowledge is put to good use.
3	action	end
1	option	I'm fine, thanks.
0	section	Talking to Seth
1	line	Seth Groats	Well well, what can I do for you?
1	line	Player	I was wondering if you could teach me a little about how you're so successful with your animals.
1	line	Seth Groats	Lookin' to get into the business, eh?
1	line	Player	Something along those lines.
1	line	Seth Groats	Well, always happy to help another budding farmer out!
1	line	Player	Great! So where do I start?
1	line	Seth Groats	Would always recommend me Groats Principles as yer basics.
1	line	Player	Groats Principles?
1	line	Seth Groats	Aye. First one is that happy animals makes happy farmers.
1	line	Seth Groats	Second of me principles is to never take more than you need. Greed'll stop you in your tracks.
1	line	Seth Groats	The last principle: never let the taxman know yer earnings. Money should be spent on the animals!
1	cond	ironman]]:
2	line	Player	I don't think I've ever paid any taxes.
2	line	Seth Groats	You're ahead of the game then!
2	action	continues
1	cond	If the player is not an ironman:
2	line	Player	You've found a way to get around the taxes?
2	line	Seth Groats	A way or two.
2	action	continues
1	line	Seth Groats	Anyway, feel free to grab me book on the topic from the shelf over there.
1	line	Player	Okay, thank you for the help.
1	action	end
