1	line	Player	Oh, that's worse milk than before.
1	line	Gillie Groats	That looked like a horrible experience.
1	line	Player	It wasn't pleasant.
1	line	Gillie Groats	Where did you even get that milk?
1	line	Player	My business partner, Cassius. I don't know where he gets it from originally though.
1	line	Gillie Groats	Cassius... I don't recognise the name. He's not mentioned anything about its source?
1	line	Player	Nothing, but he apparently has enough of a source to start a business. I'm mostly trying to be helpful.
1	line	Player	If the milk's bad, you're not going to recommend us for a permit, are you?
1	line	Gillie Groats	With how bad it looks, you wouldn't be any competition to us.
1	line	Gillie Groats	However, I wonder if I'd be doing a public service by protecting anyone else from it.
1	line	Player	Is there anything more I could do to convince you?
1	line	Gillie Groats	Now that you mention it, I've had an incredibly aggressive bull disrupting my herd lately. I've got him caught in the pen over there.
1	line	Gillie Groats	Perhaps you'd be interested in dealing with him? I'd owe you a fairly large favour.
1	line	Player	A roughly permit sized favour?
1	line	Gillie Groats	Absolutely.
1	action	end
